{"body":"## Problem\n\nReviewer compliance audit already receives the exact prompts actually dispatched to Standards/Spec children through `ReviewerAgentAttempt.prompt`, together with the canonical Skill, opaque task, execution record, child reports, and candidate Receipt. This correctly catches malformed leg prompts—but only **after** the unique sibling batch has run. A post-run prompt defect therefore forces a whole-invocation `refused`; the batch cannot lawfully be rerun.\n\n## Existence evidence — issue #15 migration review\n\nFour fresh invocations showed three distinct cases:\n\n1. task accidentally prohibited the Reviewer’s full `npm test` choice;\n2. task’s executable allowlist accidentally omitted required `PI_*` environment inspection;\n3. Reviewer-generated Standards child prompt abbreviated the mandatory canonical Fowler smell definitions/remedies; existing method audit caught this only after both children finished;\n4. after explicitly requiring the full baseline, Reviewer completed and returned substantive findings.\n\nOnly case 3 is a Reviewer prompt-construction defect. Cases 1–2 show that free-text executable policy can also make an otherwise useful batch irrecoverably invalid.\n\nDurable procedural refusals are under `.ak/dockets/issues/15/review/review-{001,002,003}/` on the issue-15 migration branch.\n\n## Direction for later Authority discussion\n\nMove correctness earlier at the Reviewer dispatch seam instead of adding another post-hoc model review:\n\n- Reviewer declares structured axes, fixed base/target, task/material identities, and executable policy;\n- runtime deterministically compiles the complete Standards/Spec prompts from the canonical Skill and task;\n- atomically preflight both prompts before either child starts;\n- reject/correct pre-dispatch without consuming the exactly-once sibling batch;\n- retain the existing post-run auditor to prove actual prompt == compiled prompt, target traceability, axis isolation, and faithful aggregation;\n- durably bind each exact prompt or deterministic recipe/version plus SHA-256.\n\n## Boundaries to adjudicate\n\n- whether to narrow the existing `Agent` interface or add one atomic batch-dispatch interface;\n- what can be mechanically checked versus audited semantically;\n- how executable policy avoids both over-broad access and impossible allowlists;\n- rejected preflight attempts must not count as a started sibling batch;\n- no Reviewer Soul duplication of prompt templates, schemas, CLI mechanics, or Fowler text;\n- no change to caller-owned review ordering/repetition or role topology.\n\n## Non-action\n\nDo not implement this inside issue #15 Case-A migration. Finish that migration against its current fixed content target first.\n","state":"OPEN","title":"Preflight Reviewer leg prompts before consuming the exactly-once sibling batch","url":"https://github.com/Akagilnc/ak-pi-workflow-roles/issues/17"}
